      <h3>Your public fork</h3>
      <p>Submit the URL to your public fork of the Canteen Chaos repository, including your fixes and a <code>LOG.md</code> with reproduction steps, root-cause analysis, and why your changes belong where you made them.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="submission-card build-card">
      <span class="task-label">Task 2 · Build</span>
      <h3>Your Gym Slot Booking repository</h3>
      <p>Submit your repository with meaningful commit history and a README. Include your stack/data-model note (10 lines maximum), assumptions, setup instructions, and admin/member test credentials. If deployed, include live links.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="integrity-note"><strong>Before submitting:</strong> make your repository public. Do not commit secrets; use environment variables and include an <code>.env.example</code>.</p>
</section>

